# ===== Target-specific extras =====
# fuzz_lexer-specific extras — lexical edge cases not covered by the
# shared base. The lexer is driven by logos; these shapes target
# byte-level branch conditions in crates/cyrs-syntax/src/kind.rs and
# the escape-handling paths in the string-literal rules.
#
# Note: libFuzzer's dictionary parser only accepts \xNN, \\, and \"
# escapes — not \n / \t / \r / \u — so raw whitespace bytes are spelled
# as \x09 / \x0a / \x0d and Unicode codepoints as their UTF-8 bytes.

# String escapes — every escape class the lexer recognises.
# These ARE source-level escapes (backslash followed by a letter), so
# libFuzzer-side each `\\` decodes to a single backslash byte.
